# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is LF in the repository and LF in every checkout. Without this
# a Windows checkout converts on the way out, each file then shows up as a
# whole-file diff (LICENSE was "modified" before a single line of code existed),
# and a shell script committed from that checkout dies in CI with
# `$'\r': command not found`.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf`: decide text vs binary by content, check text out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception: cmd.exe misparses labels and
# multi-line blocks in an LF-only script.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Fixture corpus for the readers and writers: real files whose bytes are
# compared exactly, so nothing may touch them. This includes the text fixtures
# with CRLF, UTF-16 and single-byte encodings, which the LF rule above would
# otherwise rewrite on checkout.
tests/e2e/fixtures/** binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pptx binary
*.ppsx binary
*.doc binary
*.xls binary
*.ppt binary
*.pps binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
